 Dominated coloring in certain networks, Soft Computing, Springer (2024).--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nALIKHANI, GHANBARI: INTRODUCTION TO TOTAL DOMINATOR EDGE CHROMATIC ... 797 (https://jaem.isikun.edu.tr/web/images/articles/vol.12.no.3/02.pdf)\\nciteturn0search15 [wordlim: 200] Published: 4.4 years ago; [3] Alikhani, S., Ghanbari, N., (2018), Total dominator chromatic number of some operations on a graph, Bull.\\nThe total dominator edge chromatic number (briefly TDEC-number) \\\\(\\\\chi_d^t(G)\\\\) of \\\\(G\\\\) is the minimum number of color classes in a TDE-coloring of \\\\(G\\\\). We obtained some properties of \\\\(\\\\chi_d^t(G)\\\\) and computed this parameter for specific graphs. We also examined the effects on \\\\(\\\\chi_d^t(G)\\\\) when \\\\(G\\\\) is modified by operations on vertices and edges of \\\\(G\\\\). Finally, we investigated TDEC-number of the \\\\(k\\\\)-subdivision of \\\\(G\\\\).\\n\\n## REFERENCES\\n\\n[1] Alikhani, S., Ghanbari, N., Soltani, S., Total dominator chromatic number of \\\\(k\\\\)-subdivision of graphs, submitted. Available at https://arxiv.org/abs/1801.06500.\\n\\n[2] Alikhani, S., Ghanbari, N., (2019), More on the total dominator chromatic number of a graph, J. Inform. Optim. Sci., 40, (1), pp. 157-169.\\n\\n[3] Alikhani, S., Ghanbari, N., (2018), Total dominator chromatic number of some operations on a graph, Bull. Comp. Appl. Math., 6, (2), pp. 9-20.\\n\\n[4] Henning, M. A., (2015), Total dominator colorings and total domination in graphs, Graphs Combin., 31, pp. 953–974.\\n\\n[5] Vijayalekshmi, A., (2012), Total dominator colorings in Graphs, Int. J. Adv. Research Tech., 4, pp. 1-6.\\n\\n[6] Vijayalekshmi, A., (2012), Total dominator colorings in Paths, Int. J. Math. Combin., 2, pp. 89-95.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\\nIntroduction to dominated edge chromatic number of a graph (https://www.opuscula.agh.edu.pl/vo